              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^+
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z^+
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mo +
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z^+ \times Z^+
          %p
            Given sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of this set of prefunctions between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %h3#in_type_theory In type theory
          %p
            In many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations
            based on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            come equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            which behaves similarly as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            does in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presets"} presets
            in the strict sense, in that the latter do not carry any equality at all. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            between such sets are also not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prefunctions"} prefunctions
            because
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+application+on+identifications"} function application on identifications
            implies that functions preserve
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identifications"} identifications
          %p
            However, there is a way to formalize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presets"} presets
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prefunctions"} prefunctions
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            even with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"} propositional equality
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y \coloneqq \mathrm{isContr}(\mathrm{Id}_A(x, y))
          %p
            Expanding out the definition of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification"} identification
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contraction"} contraction
            showing that the identification is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center+of+contraction"} center of contraction
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
          %p
            By this definition of equality, propositional equality is always a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isContr"} isContr
            is always a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            are unique (i.e. there is a function
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Id}_A(x, y) \to x = y
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"} propositional equality
            for unique identifications and the relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
            for the type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isContr}(\mathrm{Id}_A(x, y))
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            is then precisely a type where all identifications are unique. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+of+identity+proofs"} uniqueness of identity proofs
            states that all identity types are propositions and all identifications are unique.
          %p
            Propositional equality satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+substitution"} principle of substitution
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
            of the unique identification across
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicates"} predicates
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+of+indiscernibles"} identity of indiscernibles
            because propositional equality is always a proposition, and so we have:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:A} \mathrm{isContr}(\mathrm{Id}_A(x, y)) \simeq \prod_{x:A \to \mathrm{Prop}} P(x) \simeq P(y)
          %p
            However, propositional equality is not an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            because it is not a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+type"} loop space type
            which is not a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isContr}(\mathrm{Id}_A(x, x))
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+K"} axiom K
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presets"} presets
          %p
            Furthermore, every function can still be interpreted as a
            %strong prefunction
            in the following sense: while functions do preserve identifications, they do not preserve propositional equality in the sense of the uniqueness of identifications.
            %em Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification"} identification
            is given by a function out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+type"} interval type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\mathrm{Id}_\mathbb{I}(0, 1)
            in the interval type is unique in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi 𝕀
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Id}_\mathbb{I}(0, 1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+of+identity+proofs"} uniqueness of identity proofs
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+function"} extensional function
            as one that does preserve the uniqueness of identifications, and prove that functions between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            preserve the uniqueness of identifications, and that h-sets are precisely the types between which all functions preserve uniqueness of identifications. To say that all functions are extensional along the lines of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preset"} preset
            approach to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+of+identity+proofs"} uniqueness of identity proofs
            that implies that all types are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
          %h2#categorical_semantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            The difference between functions and prefunctions in sets is modeled in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"}> categorical semantics
            ) as the difference between a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U:C \to Set
            which is not faithful.
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preset"} preset
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"}> type theory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"} propositional equality
